<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<hick:doc xmlns:hick="http://www.hickorydocs.com/1.0">

## Shared Configuration

These files are shared across all platforms.

### EditorConfig

EditorConfig ensures consistent formatting across different editors and IDEs.
This is especially important for cross-platform projects where team members
may use different tools:

<hick:copy id="editorconfig"># EditorConfig helps maintain consistent coding styles
root = true

[*]
indent_style = space
indent_size = 2
end_of_line = lf
charset = utf-8
trim_trailing_whitespace = true
insert_final_newline = true

[*.md]
trim_trailing_whitespace = false

[*.{rs,swift}]
indent_size = 4

[*.{kt,java}]
indent_size = 4

[*.cs]
indent_size = 4

[Makefile]
indent_style = tab
</hick:copy>

<hick:file path=".editorconfig"><hick:paste select="#editorconfig" /></hick:file>

Language-specific indentation:
- **2 spaces** — JavaScript, TypeScript, JSON, YAML (web ecosystem standard)
- **4 spaces** — Rust, Swift, Kotlin, Java, C# (native ecosystem standard)
- **Tabs** — Makefiles (required by make)

### GitHub Actions CI

The CI workflow runs builds and tests for all enabled platforms. Each platform
gets its own job for parallel execution:

<hick:when test="swiftui || compose || avalonia || spa || extension || backend">
<hick:file path=".github/workflows/ci.yml">name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main, master]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main, master]

jobs:
<hick:when test="swiftui">
  apple:
    runs-on: macos-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Build iOS
        run: |
          cd apple
          xcodebuild -scheme MyProject -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 15' build

      - name: Build macOS
        run: |
          cd apple
          xcodebuild -scheme MyProject -destination 'platform=macOS' build
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="compose">
  android:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Set up JDK 17
        uses: actions/setup-java@v4
        with:
          java-version: '17'
          distribution: 'temurin'

      - name: Build Android
        run: |
          cd android
          ./gradlew assembleDebug
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="avalonia">
  desktop:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup .NET
        uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v4
        with:
          dotnet-version: '<hick:val name="dotnet_version" />'

      - name: Build Desktop
        run: |
          cd desktop
          dotnet build
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="spa">
  web:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '<hick:val name="node_version" />'
          cache: 'npm'
          cache-dependency-path: web/package-lock.json

      - name: Build Web
        run: |
          cd web
          npm ci
          npm run build
          npm run lint
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="extension">
  extension:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '<hick:val name="node_version" />'
          cache: 'npm'
          cache-dependency-path: extension/package-lock.json

      - name: Build Extension
        run: |
          cd extension
          npm ci
          npm run build
          npm run lint
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="backend">
  backend:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Rust
        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@nightly

      - name: Cache Rust
        uses: Swatinem/rust-cache@v2
        with:
          workspaces: backend

      - name: Build Backend
        run: |
          cd backend
          cargo build

      - name: Test Backend
        run: |
          cd backend
          cargo test
</hick:when>
</hick:file>
</hick:when>

CI configuration highlights:
- **Parallel jobs** — Each platform builds independently
- **Caching** — npm and Rust dependencies are cached for faster builds
- **Platform-appropriate runners** — macOS for Apple, Ubuntu for others

</hick:doc>
